<article class="env-lemma" id="02Q3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02Q3">Lemma <span data-tag="02Q3">42.68.34</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $a, b \in A$. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to M \to M' \to M'' \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> be a short exact sequence of $A$-modules of dimension $1$ such that $a, b$ are nonzerodivisors on all three $A$-modules. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  d_{M'}(a, b) = d_ M(a, b) d_{M''}(a, b)  \]
</div>
  <p> in $\kappa ^*$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is easy to see that this leads to a short exact sequence of exact $(2, 1)$-periodic complexes 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to (M/abM, a, b) \to (M'/abM', a, b) \to (M''/abM'', a, b) \to 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Hence the lemma follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/02PO" data-tag="02PO">42.68.18</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>